	(text "R69 and C52 tie the USB\nshield to GND. C52 is\n100 V: an 8 kV contact\ndischarge into the shield\nleaves about 55 V on it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "117775e4-f546-4cbf-a20f-45d277a0a96f")
	)
	(text "USB is for bench programming and debugging only. VBUS also feeds the\nAP3012 boost on the Power sheet, whose inductor and diode connect it\nstraight to VIN's capacitance (about 70 uF). The plug-in inrush therefore\nexceeds the USB limit of 10 uF. Most ports tolerate this; if one trips\nits current limit, use a powered hub.\nD24 clamps ESD and surges on VBUS. Keep it right at J14, before FB1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "27bfac73-beb7-4535-a3f0-82d0ffddd9b7")
	)
	(text "C67 and C68 are not decoupling. They carry the USB pair's return current\nbetween planes where the pair changes layer: it runs on In3, next to the\n+3V3 plane on In2, but starts and ends on GND-referenced layers.\nKeep C67 beside the vias next to FL1, and C68 beside the vias next to the SoM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 80.01 110.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a29cd9f5-b2e1-45e5-b0f0-647383309977")
	)
